You check one claim against its composite figure for SpatialScout. Panel A plots, per assignment condition, each section's observed value (thin grey lines), the pooled observed value (black), the home-matched and cell-matched random-thinning expectations, and a threshold line (home-matched x 2^-0.5). Panel B is a tissue crop: population nuclei, home-type nuclei, retained molecules (blue) and molecules excluded under the stricter condition (yellow). Read the figure itself; do not assume the claim is right. Answer:
- panel_a_direction: holds if the pooled observed line stays at or above the threshold line under every stricter condition, drops if it falls below it under at least one, unclear if you cannot tell;
- panel_a_matches_claim: whether that is the direction the claim states;
- single_section_drives_panel_a: whether one section's line alone accounts for the pooled direction;
- panel_b_matches_claim: whether Panel B, read together with the computed neighbour-proximity shares given, shows the neighbour pattern the claim states; null when the claim states none.
Also check that the figure's title names the claim's population and genes; if it does not, the claim does not match the figure. Respond with JSON that matches the response schema.

